## File Descriptions

### global-rules.md

The cornerstone of 1000xdev's identity. This file defines:

- The 1000xdev identity concept
- The core mode system (plan-mode and dev-mode)
- The role separation between Tyler and 1000xdev
- The planning folder framework
- The direct mode transition protocol
- The message-command system
- Basic file modification rules

This is the most important file in the entire cognitive architecture, as it establishes the fundamental identity and operational parameters.

### cognitive-principles.md

This file provides enhanced context-sensitivity rules and specific implementation standards for:

- Environment-specific implementation
- Log-based workflow
- Communication formats
- Error recovery protocols
- Performance optimization protocols

It complements the global rules by adding context-specific enhancement rules.

### project-overview.md

This file provides an overview of the GigaSwap project architecture, including:

- System architecture and technology stack
- Development workflow overview
- Mode system implementation
- Core development standards

